# R4 — One source of truth per contract

The `WorldAPI` (`SetSkyState`, `AdvanceTime`, `SpawnTrees`, …) is defined
**once** in `packages/world-api/`. All other languages (Python brain,
Unreal C++/Blueprint) consume **generated** artefacts. No hand-maintained
parallel definitions anywhere else.

This makes contract drift impossible: change the TS source, regenerate,
every consumer breaks at compile-time until updated.

> Status (2026-06-01): `packages/world-api/` is created in Task 0.3. The
> generator pipeline (TS → Python via JSON Schema or `pydantic`-from-zod,
> TS → UE C++ via a small codegen) is built in Phase 2.

## ❌ BAD

```py
# packages/llm-brain/src/tools.py — DO NOT hand-maintain
class SetSkyStateArgs(BaseModel):
    preset: Literal["clear", "cloudy", "storm", "sunset", "night"]
    transition_seconds: float = 5.0
```

## ✅ GOOD

```py
# Generated by `pnpm gen:types` from packages/world-api/src/contract.ts
# DO NOT EDIT — re-run codegen instead.
from yellow_ue.world_api.generated import SetSkyStateArgs
```

## When you need to add or change a world-API tool

1. Edit `packages/world-api/src/contract.ts` (single source).
2. Run `pnpm gen:types` (regenerates Python + UE bindings).
3. Update consumers — TypeScript will fail compile, Python `mypy` will
   complain, UE Blueprint will show a red node. Fix them.
4. Update the corresponding inspector page (see R5).

If you find a definition of a contract type *outside* `packages/world-api/`
that is **not** marked "Generated by codegen", delete it and replace with
an import of the generated version.
